config ZRAM_EXT
	tristate "Compressed RAM block device with writeback (zram_ext)"
	depends on ZRAM && m
	select ZSMALLOC
	help
	  A copy of the zram driver, built as the zram_ext module with
	  writeback to a backing device, per-slot access time tracking and
	  recompression with secondary algorithms always enabled. GKI builds
	  zram.ko without CONFIG_ZRAM_WRITEBACK, CONFIG_ZRAM_MEMORY_TRACKING
	  and (on 6.1) recompression, and a vendor module cannot change that,
	  so devices that need them load zram_ext.ko instead of zram.ko. Both
	  register the same block device and the same zram-control class:
	  only one of them can be loaded.

	  The default compressor is the one chosen for ZRAM.

	  See Documentation/admin-guide/blockdev/zram.rst for the interface.
